This product includes research-workflow capabilities (deep research and auto
research) that were adapted from, and inspired by, the following open projects.
We are grateful to their authors.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Feynman (feynman.is)
    Companion, Inc.  —  https://github.com/companion-inc/feynman
    License: MIT

    The skills under `.claude/skills/deep-research-candidates/` and
    `.claude/skills/auto-research-loop/` adapt the workflow discipline of
    Feynman's `/deepresearch` and `/autoresearch` prompt templates:
    the plan -> gather -> draft -> cite -> verify -> deliver sequence, the
    bounded hypothesize -> experiment -> measure -> decide loop, the
    `outputs/.plans` / `outputs/.drafts` artifact layout, and the
    `<slug>.provenance.md` provenance sidecar. Artifact names
    (`autoresearch.md`, `autoresearch.jsonl`) are kept for continuity with a
    Feynman install. Feynman is bundled in this repo under `.agents/skills/feynman/`.

    MIT License text: https://github.com/companion-inc/feynman/blob/main/LICENSE

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OpenResearch CLI (orx)
    alphaXiv  —  https://github.com/alphaXiv/openresearch-cli

    Three concepts are adapted (as design, not copied code):
      - the experiment tree (baseline = root, each variant a child measured
        against its parent, "grow down, not sideways" = descend onto winners),
        implemented in `src/autoengineering/research/experiment.py`;
      - multi-hop literature search (fetch a paper, extract its references,
        fetch those, repeat), described in
        `.claude/skills/multi-hop-lit-search/`;
      - evidence-first reporting (lead with measured evidence before
        conclusions), implemented in `src/autoengineering/research/provenance.py`.

    Note: no LICENSE file was detectable in that repository at integration time.
    Only concepts were adapted here; no source code was copied. If verbatim reuse
    is later desired, confirm the upstream license first.
